var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"core_data/#Market-data","page":"Market data","text":"Asset holds one instrument's OHLC-style price matrix and indicator columns; Market is a collection of Assets keyed by ticker. Bar advancement is zero-copy — see advance_to!.\n\nPages = [\"core_data.md\"]","title":"Market data"},{"category":"type","location":"core_data/#Orcus.Asset","page":"Market data","text":"Asset\n\nA single instrument's price/indicator data.\n\ndata is an AbstractMatrix{Float64} with shape [n_datasets × n_bars]. During a backtest the broker's assets hold a SubArray view into the base market data — zero-copy bar advancement. Outside the loop (and after copy) it is always a concrete Matrix{Float64}.\n\nNaN is used as the sentinel for missing/gap bars — no Union boxing. Indexing by an absent dataset name throws KeyError; name reads return concrete Vector{Float64} (window slice) or Float64 (scalar).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.Asset"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.add_datapoint!-Tuple{Asset, Vector{Float64}}","page":"Market data","text":"add_datapoint!(A::Asset, dp::DataPoint)\n\nAppend a new bar (column) to the asset, recomputing indicator rows.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.add_datapoint!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.apply_indicator-Tuple{IndicatorGenerator, Asset, String, String}","page":"Market data","text":"apply_indicator(Ind, asset, data_key, name)\n\nCompute and attach a named indicator row to the asset. Must be called in init, not next (asset.data may be a view during backtest).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.apply_indicator"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.calculate_indicator-Tuple{IndicatorGenerator, Asset, String}","page":"Market data","text":"calculate_indicator(Ind, asset, data_key)\n\nCompute an indicator series over the asset's named column. NaN bars in the source propagate as NaN in the output.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.calculate_indicator"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.rand_ohlc-Tuple{Number, Function, StepRange{Int64, Int64}, Int64}","page":"Market data","text":"rand_ohlc(base, f, interval, precision) -> (DataSeries, Vector{String})\n\nGenerate synthetic OHLC bars. Non-sampled bars are filled with NaN.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.rand_ohlc"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.rowindex-Tuple{Asset, String}","page":"Market data","text":"rowindex(A::Asset, name::String) -> Int\n\nRow index of the named series (0 if absent). Resolve once (e.g. in a strategy's init) and read with the integer accessor A[row, col] to skip the per-call String hash on the hot path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.rowindex"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.shorten!-Tuple{Asset, UnitRange{Int64}}","page":"Market data","text":"shorten!(A::Asset, u::UnitRange{Int})\n\nTrim asset data to the given column range (materializes views).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.shorten!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.value-Tuple{Asset}","page":"Market data","text":"value(A::Asset, data_key=\"Close\")\n\nCurrent price: last non-NaN value in the named row. O(1) for clean CSV data (no NaN at end), O(n_gaps) for sparse synthetic data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.value"},{"category":"type","location":"core_data/#Orcus.Market","page":"Market data","text":"Market\n\nA collection of Assets keyed by ticker. _length caches the maximum bar count so length(M) is O(1) instead of scanning all assets every call.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.Market"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.advance_to!-Tuple{Market, Int64}","page":"Market data","text":"advance_to!(M, i)\n\nReveal bars 1:i of every asset by moving its visible cursor — O(N_assets) integer writes, zero allocation. Each asset already holds its full price matrix; advancing the cursor is what the backtest loop does once per bar (replaces the old SubArray view churn).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.advance_to!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.asset_names-Tuple{Market}","page":"Market data","text":"asset_names(M::Market) -> Vector{String}\n\nSorted ticker names — stable ordering for cross-sectional matrix rows.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.asset_names"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.returns_matrix-Tuple{Market, UnitRange{Int64}}","page":"Market data","text":"returns_matrix(M, window; key=\"Close\") -> Matrix{Float64}\n\n[N × (T-1)] log-return matrix. Rows = assets (alpha order), cols = bars. NaN/zero prices fill the corresponding column with 0.0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.returns_matrix"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.set_data_to!-Tuple{Market, Market, UnitRange{Int64}}","page":"Market data","text":"set_data_to!(M, N, u)\n\nBack-compat shim for the old view-based API: advances M to reveal bars 1:last(u) via the visible cursor (M already holds the full series). N is ignored. Prefer advance_to!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.set_data_to!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.trim_to_length-Tuple{Market, Int64}","page":"Market data","text":"trim_to_length(M, n) -> Market\n\nNew Market where every asset is trimmed to its last n bars.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.trim_to_length"},{"category":"type","location":"core_data/#Orcus.IndicatorGenerator","page":"Market data","text":"IndicatorGenerator(f::Function,window::Int)\n\nFields\n\nf: computation function\nwindow: lookback size\n\nExample\n\nSMA10=indicator_generator(simple_average,10)\nSMA10.window\n\n# output\n10\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.IndicatorGenerator"},{"category":"method","location":"core_data/#Orcus.simple_average-Tuple{Vector{Float64}}","page":"Market data","text":"simple_average([1,missing,3,4])\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.simple_average"},{"category":"section","location":"analytics/#Analytics","page":"Analytics","text":"Rolling PCA factor models, rolling-window statistics, backtest performance metrics, technical indicators, and option-pricing helpers.\n\nPages = [\"analytics.md\"]","title":"Analytics"},{"category":"type","location":"analytics/#Orcus.RollingPCA","page":"Analytics","text":"RollingPCA(window, n_factors)\n\nRolling PCA factor model. Maintains top n_factors eigenvectors of the return covariance matrix, estimated over a sliding window of bars.\n\nFields set after fit!:\n\neigvecs — [N × K] matrix, columns are factor loadings (descending variance)\neigvals — K eigenvalues (descending)\nfitted  — false until first fit! call\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.RollingPCA"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.explained_variance-Tuple{RollingPCA}","page":"Analytics","text":"explained_variance(pca::RollingPCA) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nFraction of total variance explained by each factor (sums to ≤ 1). Length equals n_factors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.explained_variance"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.fit!-Tuple{RollingPCA, Matrix{Float64}}","page":"Analytics","text":"fit!(pca::RollingPCA, R::Matrix{Float64})\n\nFit PCA on return matrix R of shape [N × T].  Stores the top K eigenvectors (by variance explained) and their eigenvalues.  Requires T ≥ 2 and N ≥ n_factors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.fit!"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.plot_residual_corr-Tuple{Matrix{Float64}, Vector{String}}","page":"Analytics","text":"plot_residual_corr(E::Matrix{Float64}, names::Vector{String})\n\nPrint the residual correlation matrix as a formatted table. Returns the [N × N] correlation matrix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.plot_residual_corr"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.project-Tuple{RollingPCA, Matrix{Float64}}","page":"Analytics","text":"project(pca::RollingPCA, R::Matrix{Float64}) -> (F, E)\n\nBatch projection of return matrix R [N × T]. Returns factor matrix F [K × T] and residual matrix E [N × T].\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.project"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.project-Tuple{RollingPCA, Vector{Float64}}","page":"Analytics","text":"project(pca::RollingPCA, r::Vector{Float64}) -> (factors, residuals)\n\nProject a single bar's return vector r [N] through the fitted PCA. Returns:\n\nfactors   — [K] factor returns (projection onto eigenvectors)\nresiduals — [N] idiosyncratic residual after removing factor component\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.project"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.residual_corr-Tuple{Matrix{Float64}}","page":"Analytics","text":"residual_corr(E::Matrix{Float64}) -> Matrix{Float64}\n\n[N × N] Pearson correlation matrix of the residual rows. After good PCA factorization this should be close to the identity matrix — off-diagonal entries indicate remaining common structure.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.residual_corr"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.rolling_mean-Tuple{Vector{Float64}, Int64}","page":"Analytics","text":"rolling_mean(v, w) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nRolling mean of v with window w. First w-1 entries are NaN.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.rolling_mean"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.rolling_std-Tuple{Vector{Float64}, Int64}","page":"Analytics","text":"rolling_std(v, w) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nRolling standard deviation of v with window w. First w-1 entries are NaN.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.rolling_std"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.rolling_zscore-Tuple{Vector{Float64}, Int64}","page":"Analytics","text":"rolling_zscore(v, w) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nRolling z-score of v with window w: (v[i] - mean(v[i-w+1:i])) / std(...). First w-1 entries are NaN. Bars with zero local standard deviation are NaN.\n\nCan also be used as an IndicatorGenerator function:\n\napply_indicator(IndicatorGenerator(rolling_zscore, 30), asset, \"Close\", \"ZScore30\")\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.rolling_zscore"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.annualized_return-Tuple{Vector{<:Real}}","page":"Analytics","text":"annualized_return(equity; periods_per_year=252) -> Float64\n\nCompound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR): the constant yearly return that would produce the same total growth as the equity curve.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.annualized_return"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.backtest_summary-Tuple{Backtest}","page":"Analytics","text":"backtest_summary(bt::Backtest)\n\nPrint a concise performance summary for a completed backtest.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.backtest_summary"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.bah_equity-Tuple{Market, Real}","page":"Analytics","text":"bah_equity(market, cash; key=\"Close\") -> Vector{Float64}\n\nCompute the equity curve of an equal-weight buy-and-hold strategy across all assets in market from bar 1 onward. Useful as a benchmark for information_ratio and compare_backtests.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.bah_equity"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.calmar_ratio-Tuple{Vector{<:Real}}","page":"Analytics","text":"calmar_ratio(equity; periods_per_year=252) -> Float64\n\nAnnualized return divided by maximum drawdown.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.calmar_ratio"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.compare_backtests-Tuple{Vector{<:Backtest}, Vector{String}}","page":"Analytics","text":"compare_backtests(bts, names; benchmark=nothing)\n\nPrint a side-by-side performance table for a collection of backtests. Columns: Strategy | CAGR | Sharpe | Sortino | Calmar | Omega | VaR95 | MaxDD | Trades. Pass benchmark (equity curve) to append an Information Ratio column.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.compare_backtests"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.cross_section_rank-Tuple{Vector{Float64}}","page":"Analytics","text":"cross_section_rank(v) -> Vector{Int}\n\nInteger ranks 1…N (1 = smallest value). Useful for factor-based long/short construction.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.cross_section_rank"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.cross_section_zscore-Tuple{Vector{Float64}}","page":"Analytics","text":"cross_section_zscore(v) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nNormalize a cross-sectional score vector to zero mean and unit variance. Returns zeros if the vector has zero standard deviation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.cross_section_zscore"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.cvar-Tuple{Vector{<:Real}}","page":"Analytics","text":"cvar(equity; confidence=0.95) -> Float64\n\nConditional Value at Risk (Expected Shortfall): the mean return on the worst (1-confidence) fraction of days. More conservative than VaR. Returned as a negative number.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.cvar"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.extended_summary-Tuple{Backtest}","page":"Analytics","text":"extended_summary(bt::Backtest; benchmark=nothing)\n\nPrint a detailed performance summary including CAGR, Sortino, Calmar, Omega, VaR, CVaR, and Ulcer Index. Pass a benchmark equity curve (e.g. from bah_equity) to also print the Information Ratio.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.extended_summary"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.information_ratio-Tuple{Vector{<:Real}, Vector{<:Real}}","page":"Analytics","text":"information_ratio(equity, benchmark_equity; periods_per_year=252) -> Float64\n\nInformation Ratio: annualised active return divided by tracking error vs a benchmark equity curve. Measures skill of active management. Values above 0.5 are considered good; above 1.0 exceptional.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.information_ratio"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.max_drawdown-Tuple{Vector{<:Real}}","page":"Analytics","text":"max_drawdown(equity) -> Float64\n\nMaximum peak-to-trough drawdown as a fraction (0 to 1).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.max_drawdown"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.omega_ratio-Tuple{Vector{<:Real}}","page":"Analytics","text":"omega_ratio(equity; threshold=0.0, periods_per_year=252) -> Float64\n\nOmega ratio: probability-weighted ratio of gains to losses above/below threshold (annualised). Values > 1 indicate more gain than loss. Unlike Sharpe, Omega uses the full return distribution (captures skew/kurtosis).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.omega_ratio"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.profit_factor-Tuple{Vector{<:Real}}","page":"Analytics","text":"profit_factor(equity) -> Float64\n\nGross profit / gross loss computed from the equity-curve return series. Returns Inf if there are no losing bars.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.profit_factor"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.sharpe_ratio-Tuple{Vector{<:Real}}","page":"Analytics","text":"sharpe_ratio(equity; rf=0.0, periods_per_year=252) -> Float64\n\nAnnualized Sharpe ratio computed from an equity curve. rf is the annualized risk-free rate (default 0). Returns NaN if there is insufficient data or zero volatility.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.sharpe_ratio"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.sortino_ratio-Tuple{Vector{<:Real}}","page":"Analytics","text":"sortino_ratio(equity; rf=0.0, periods_per_year=252) -> Float64\n\nAnnualized Sortino ratio: like Sharpe but penalises downside volatility only. Downside deviation = sqrt(mean of squared negative excess returns).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.sortino_ratio"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.ulcer_index-Tuple{Vector{<:Real}}","page":"Analytics","text":"ulcer_index(equity) -> Float64\n\nUlcer Index: root mean square of all percentage drawdowns from peak. Captures both depth and duration of drawdowns. Lower is better. Useful as a risk denominator (Martin Ratio = CAGR / Ulcer Index).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.ulcer_index"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.value_at_risk-Tuple{Vector{<:Real}}","page":"Analytics","text":"value_at_risk(equity; confidence=0.95) -> Float64\n\nDaily Value at Risk at the given confidence level: the return threshold such that losses exceed this level on (1-confidence) fraction of days. Returned as a negative number (a loss).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.value_at_risk"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.win_rate_bars-Tuple{Vector{<:Real}}","page":"Analytics","text":"win_rate_bars(equity) -> Float64\n\nFraction of bars in which the equity curve increased (a rough proxy for trade-level win rate when the strategy has one position at a time).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.win_rate_bars"},{"category":"function","location":"analytics/#Orcus.atr","page":"Analytics","text":"atr(high, low, close, w=14) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nAverage True Range using Wilder's smoothing. True Range = max(H-L, |H-prevC|, |L-prevC|). Returns NaN for the first w+1 bars. Not directly IndicatorGenerator-compatible (needs three input series); call directly in strategy logic:\n\nh = Float64.(asset[\"High\"]); l = Float64.(asset[\"Low\"]); c = Float64.(asset[\"Close\"])\natr_val = last(filter(!isnan, atr(h, l, c, 14)))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.atr"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.ema-Tuple{Vector{Float64}, Int64}","page":"Analytics","text":"ema(v, w) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nExponential moving average with span w (α = 2/(w+1)). Initialised with the SMA of the first w bars; NaN for earlier entries. Compatible with IndicatorGenerator:\n\napply_indicator(IndicatorGenerator(ema, 20), asset, \"Close\", \"EMA20\")\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.ema"},{"category":"function","location":"analytics/#Orcus.rsi","page":"Analytics","text":"rsi(v, w=14) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nRelative Strength Index using Wilder's smoothing. Returns values in [0, 100]; NaN for the first w bars. Compatible with IndicatorGenerator:\n\napply_indicator(IndicatorGenerator(rsi, 14), asset, \"Close\", \"RSI14\")\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.rsi"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.bsm_call-NTuple{5, Float64}","page":"Analytics","text":"bsm_call(S, K, T, r, sigma) -> Float64\n\nBlack-Scholes-Merton European call price.\n\nS     current underlying price\nK     strike\nT     time to expiry in years (e.g., 21/252 for one month)\nr     risk-free rate (annualized, e.g., 0.04)\nsigma annualized volatility (e.g., 0.20)\n\nReturns intrinsic value max(S-K, 0) when T ≤ 0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.bsm_call"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.bsm_delta-NTuple{5, Float64}","page":"Analytics","text":"bsm_delta(S, K, T, r, sigma; type=:call) -> Float64\n\nBlack-Scholes-Merton option delta. type is :call (default) or :put. Call delta ∈ (0, 1); put delta ∈ (-1, 0).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.bsm_delta"},{"category":"method","location":"analytics/#Orcus.bsm_put-NTuple{5, Float64}","page":"Analytics","text":"bsm_put(S, K, T, r, sigma) -> Float64\n\nBlack-Scholes-Merton European put price (via put-call parity).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.bsm_put"},{"category":"function","location":"analytics/#Orcus.realized_vol","page":"Analytics","text":"realized_vol(prices, window=20) -> Float64\n\nAnnualized realized volatility estimated from the last window log-returns of a price series. Returns NaN if insufficient data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.realized_vol"},{"category":"section","location":"core_backtest/#Backtesting","page":"Backtesting","text":"Backtest/run_test drive the bar-by-bar loop; batch_backtest runs a threaded parameter sweep (see the module docs on per-job market isolation); the Tables.jl collectors derive Tables.jl row tables lazily from backtest output.\n\nPages = [\"core_backtest.md\"]","title":"Backtesting"},{"category":"type","location":"core_backtest/#Orcus.Backtest","page":"Backtesting","text":"Backtest(market::Market, strategy::Strategy, cash::Real=1000)\n\nBacktest a strategy on a market.\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nx=asset();\ny=asset();\nM=market([x,y]);\nT = Backtest(M,CrossOverStrategy,1000)\nrun_test(T)\n\n# output\n\nBacktest of CrossOverStrategy with 375.71 funds on market comprised of 2 assets.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.Backtest"},{"category":"method","location":"core_backtest/#Orcus.batch_backtest-Tuple{Any, Integer}","page":"Backtesting","text":"batch_backtest(builder, n; threaded=true, progress=false) -> Vector{Backtest}\n\nLower-level form: run n jobs where builder(i) returns an already-isolated Backtest (its own copied or freshly loaded market). The runner executes and collects them, but performs no implicit market copy — the builder owns isolation. Use this for sweeps that vary the universe itself rather than just strategy parameters:\n\nres = batch_backtest(length(universes)) do i\n    run_test(Backtest(market([copy(a) for a in universes[i]]), MyStrat, 10_000))\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.batch_backtest"},{"category":"method","location":"core_backtest/#Orcus.batch_backtest-Tuple{Market, Type, Real, AbstractVector}","page":"Backtesting","text":"batch_backtest(market, strategy, cash, grid; threaded=true, cost_model=NoCost(), progress=false)\n\nRun a parameter sweep of strategy over market, one backtest per entry of grid, returning a Vector{Backtest} in input order.\n\nEach job is fully isolated: the runner deep-copys market (so the shared per-asset visible cursor and any indicators attached in init are private to the job) and builds its own Backtest. With that isolation, jobs run on separate threads with no shared mutable state — the threaded result is identical to the sequential one.\n\ngrid is a vector of NamedTuples forwarded as keyword arguments to the strategy constructor. Declare the swept parameters as typed fields with @generate_strategy (or a custom @strategy_methods struct whose constructor accepts the same keywords):\n\n@generate_strategy SMAcross cross_next cross_init fast::Int=10 slow::Int=20\nres = batch_backtest(market([copy(AAPL)]), SMAcross, 10_000,\n                     [(fast=5, slow=20), (fast=10, slow=30)])\n\nKeyword arguments:\n\nthreaded  – run jobs across threads (default true; falls back to sequential when only one thread is available). Start Julia with -t auto/-t N to use more than one thread.\ncost_model – CostModel applied to every job's broker (default NoCost()).\nprogress  – when true, log elapsed time and ETA as jobs complete (default false, quiet).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.batch_backtest"},{"category":"method","location":"core_backtest/#Orcus.cashflows_table-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Backtesting","text":"cashflows_table(B::Broker)\n\nThe cash balance over time (cash_history) as a Tables.jl row table.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.cashflows_table"},{"category":"method","location":"core_backtest/#Orcus.equity_table-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Backtesting","text":"equity_table(B::Broker)\n\nThe equity curve (B.equity_history) as a Tables.jl row table.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.equity_table"},{"category":"method","location":"core_backtest/#Orcus.positions_table-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Backtesting","text":"positions_table(B::Broker)\n\nEvery open position in B.portfolio as a Tables.jl row table.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.positions_table"},{"category":"method","location":"core_backtest/#Orcus.trades_table-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Backtesting","text":"trades_table(B::Broker)\n\nEvery fill in B.history as a Tables.jl row table.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.trades_table"},{"category":"method","location":"core_backtest/#Orcus.turnover_table-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Backtesting","text":"turnover_table(B::Broker)\n\nPer-bar traded notional and turnover (traded_notional / equity) as a Tables.jl row table. Uses delta_cash rather than volume/price(T): close-out trades from resolve_portfolio! are recorded with volume == 0.0 (the cash impact is carried by delta_cash instead), so volume-based notional would silently drop every forced close.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.turnover_table"},{"category":"method","location":"core_backtest/#Orcus.weights_table-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Backtesting","text":"weights_table(B::Broker)\n\nPer-bar, per-instrument notional value and weight-of-equity as a Tables.jl row table. Replays B.history forward to rebuild net quantity per instrument over time (assets retain their full price matrix — visible is only a cursor — so historical marks are just an indexed read), then marks each open lot via payoff at that bar's Close, generic over every Derivative type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.weights_table"},{"category":"section","location":"core_strategy/#Strategy-authoring","page":"Strategy authoring","text":"A strategy is two functions registered with @generate_strategy Name next_fn init_fn:\n\ninit(s::Strategy) runs once; typically attaches indicators via apply_indicator.\nnext(s::Strategy) runs once per bar.\n\nInside both, reach the portfolio via s.broker and price data via s.market. See the Quick start for a full SMA-crossover example, and Lib for the built-in crossover_init/crossover_next strategy.\n\nPages = [\"core_strategy.md\"]","title":"Strategy authoring"},{"category":"section","location":"core_derivatives/#Derivatives","page":"Derivatives","text":"Tradeable instruments — Buy/Sell for the underlying, plus LongCall/LongPut/ ShortCall/ShortPut — dispatched through a common payoff interface.\n\nPages = [\"core_derivatives.md\"]","title":"Derivatives"},{"category":"type","location":"core_derivatives/#Orcus.Derivative","page":"Derivatives","text":"Derivative\n\nAbstract type for all derivatives.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.Derivative"},{"category":"type","location":"core_derivatives/#Orcus.InstrumentKey","page":"Derivatives","text":"instrument_key(D::Derivative)\n\nHashable identifier under which positions net. Two fills net into the same position iff their keys are equal: same ticker, same derivative type, same strike (options) and same expiry (short options). Buy and Sell on one ticker are distinct keys and do not net against each other.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.InstrumentKey"},{"category":"function","location":"core_derivatives/#Orcus.payoff","page":"Derivatives","text":"payoff(D::Derivative, x)\n\nThe derivative's payoff structure evaluated at underlying value x. Dispatched on the concrete type (no boxed Function field), so value(D) is type-stable and inlinable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.payoff"},{"category":"method","location":"core_derivatives/#Orcus.print_props-Tuple{Derivative}","page":"Derivatives","text":"print_props(D::Derivative)\n\nPrint all the current properties of the input derivative. \n\nExamples\n\nRandom.seed!(456);\nA = asset();\nB = Buy(A,10);\nprint_props(B)\n# output\n\n========================================\nAssets: KPGR\nDerivative type: Buy\nUnderlying value: 100.16749318215984\nDerivative value: 100.16749318215984\nPrice paid: 110.16749318215984\nStrike price: None\nAbsolute return: -10.0\nPercentage return: -0.09077087724475305\nLog return: -0.09515815632970726\n========================================\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.print_props"},{"category":"macro","location":"core_derivatives/#Orcus.@generate_derivative-Tuple{Symbol, Expr, Expr}","page":"Derivatives","text":"@generate_derivative(Name::Symbol, structure::Expr, price_func::Expr)\n\nMacro to generate a new derivative type.\n\nExamples\n\n@generate_derivative NewBuy x->x (val,premium)->val+premium\n\nx = asset()\nname(NewBuy(x,10))\n\n# output\n\n\"NewBuy\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.@generate_derivative"},{"category":"section","location":"lib/#Lib","page":"Lib","text":"Sample stock data loaders and an example SMA-crossover strategy.\n\nPages = [\"lib.md\"]","title":"Lib"},{"category":"method","location":"lib/#Orcus.available_stocks-Tuple{}","page":"Lib","text":"available_stocks() -> Vector{String}\n\nList all stock tickers available in the data directory.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.available_stocks"},{"category":"method","location":"lib/#Orcus.load_stock-Tuple{String}","page":"Lib","text":"load_stock(name::String)\n\nLoad the stock data from the CSV file data/<name>.csv.\n\nload_stock(\"GOOG\")\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.load_stock"},{"category":"method","location":"lib/#Orcus.load_stocks-Tuple{Vector{String}}","page":"Lib","text":"load_stocks(names::Vector{String}) -> Market\n\nLoad multiple stocks by ticker name and return them as a Market. All tickers must exist in the data directory (see available_stocks()).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.load_stocks"},{"category":"method","location":"lib/#Orcus.crossover_next-Tuple{Strategy}","page":"Lib","text":"crossover_next(s::Strategy)\n\nnext for CrossOverStrategy: closes all positions and buys 10 units on an SMA10/SMA20 upward cross, or sells 10 units on a downward cross.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.crossover_next"},{"category":"section","location":"#Orcus.jl","page":"Home","text":"A quantitative backtesting engine for Julia, focused on research and signal authoring. Write a strategy as two functions, run it bar-by-bar over historical data, and inspect the equity curve, trades, and portfolio.\n\nPages = [\"core_data.md\", \"core_accounting.md\", \"core_derivatives.md\", \"core_strategy.md\", \"core_backtest.md\", \"lib.md\", \"analytics.md\"]\nDepth = 1","title":"Orcus.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quick-start","page":"Home","text":"A strategy is two functions — init (run once) and next (run once per bar) — registered with @generate_strategy. Inside them, reach the portfolio via s.broker and the price data via s.market.\n\nusing Orcus\n\nM = market([GOOG])          # built-in sample data; see available_stocks()\n\nfunction cross_init(s::Strategy)\n    for (_, a) in s.market.data\n        apply_indicator(IndicatorGenerator(simple_average, 10), a, \"Close\", \"SMA10\")\n        apply_indicator(IndicatorGenerator(simple_average, 20), a, \"Close\", \"SMA20\")\n    end\nend\n\nfunction cross_next(s::Strategy)\n    for (_, a) in s.market.data\n        n = length(a)\n        n < 2 && continue\n        crossed_up = a[\"SMA10\", n] > a[\"SMA20\", n] && a[\"SMA10\", n-1] <= a[\"SMA20\", n-1]\n        if crossed_up\n            request_to_close_all!(s.broker)\n            place_order!(s.broker, Order(Buy(a, 5)))\n        end\n    end\nend\n\n@generate_strategy SMAcrossover cross_next cross_init\n\nbt = Backtest(M, SMAcrossover, 10_000)   # 10k starting cash\nrun_test(bt)\n\nprintln(bt)\nstatus(bt.broker)\nplot(bt)","title":"Quick start"},{"category":"section","location":"#Layout","page":"Home","text":"Core — Market data, Orders & accounting, Derivatives, Strategy authoring, Backtesting.\nLib — sample stock data loaders and example strategies.\nAnalytics — rolling PCA factor models, rolling-window statistics, technical indicators, and option-pricing helpers.","title":"Layout"},{"category":"section","location":"core_accounting/#Orders-and-accounting","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"The order/fill/accounting path: a single deterministic FIFO fill in execute!, netted Positions keyed by (ticker, type, strike, expiry), and pluggable CostModel/MarginModel applied per fill.\n\nPages = [\"core_accounting.md\"]","title":"Orders & accounting"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.Limit","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"Limit(price::Real)\n\nResting order that only fills once the bar's range reaches a price at least as good as price (in the underlying asset's own price units). Fills at the better of the bar's open and price.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.Limit"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.MarketOrder","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"MarketOrder()\n\nFills unconditionally at price(order.derivative) — the default, unchanged since before order kinds existed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.MarketOrder"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.Order","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"Order(derivative::Derivative, volume::Real=1, kind::OrderKind=MarketOrder(); allow_partial::Bool=false)\n\nAn order to buy or sell a derivative, not yet fulfilled. volume is the original requested quantity and is never mutated; remaining tracks the unfilled quantity as partial fills occur.\n\nA=asset();\nB=Buy(A,10);\nO=order(B);\nO.fulfilled\n# output\n\nfalse\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.Order"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.OrderKind","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"OrderKind\n\nAbstract type for order trigger semantics. A concrete OrderKind determines whether/at what price an Order fills on a given bar via check_trigger.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.OrderKind"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.Stop","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"Stop(price::Real)\n\nResting order that fills once the bar's range breaches price (in the underlying asset's own price units) — the mirror image of Limit. Fills at the worse of the bar's open and price.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.Stop"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.check_trigger-Union{Tuple{D}, Tuple{Order{D, MarketOrder}, Any, Int64}} where D<:Derivative","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"check_trigger(O::Order, B::Broker, date::Int) -> (triggered::Bool, fill_price::Float64)\n\nWhether O fills on bar date, and at what price. MarketOrders always trigger at price(O.derivative) — unchanged from the pre-order-kind behavior. Limit/Stop orders on Buy/Sell derivatives trigger against the underlying asset's Open/High/Low for date, using the conservative gap convention (fill at the better-of the bar's open and the trigger price).\n\nDirection (does the order want price to fall or rise to trigger?) is derived from sign(price(O.derivative)) * sign(remaining(O)): positive means this fill is a cash outflow (buy-side semantics — long entry, or short cover), negative means a cash inflow (sell-side semantics — long exit, or short entry via Sell).\n\nNot defined for other derivative types (options etc.) — their price has no per-bar repricing formula, so limit/stop orders on them raise MethodError rather than behaving silently wrong.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.check_trigger"},{"category":"function","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.fulfill","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"fulfill(order::Order,date::DateTime=now())\n\nFulfill an Order, returns the price of the Order.\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nA=asset();\nB=Buy(A,10);\nO=Order(B,10);\nfulfill(O,100)\n# output\n\n1202.1778063564075\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.fulfill"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.isfulfilled-Tuple{Order}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"isfulfilled(order::Order)\n\nReturns true if the Order has been fulfilled.\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nA=asset();\nB=Buy(A,10);\nO=Order(B,10);\nisfulfilled(O)\n# output\n\nfalse\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.isfulfilled"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.limit_order-Tuple{Derivative, Real, Real}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"limit_order(derivative, volume, price; allow_partial=false)\n\nConvenience constructor for an Order with a Limit kind.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.limit_order"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.price-Tuple{Order}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"price(order::Order,date::DateTime=now())\n\nThe price of a placed Order, can be negative.\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nA=asset();\nB=Buy(A,10);\nO=order(B,10);\nprice(O)\n# output\n\n1080.1689673025153\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.price"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.remaining-Tuple{Order}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"remaining(order::Order) -> Float64\n\nSigned quantity still unfilled on order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.remaining"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.stop_order-Tuple{Derivative, Real, Real}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"stop_order(derivative, volume, price; allow_partial=false)\n\nConvenience constructor for an Order with a Stop kind.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.stop_order"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.Trade","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"Trade(O::Order)\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nA = asset();\nB = Buy(A, 10);\nO = order(B, 100);\nT = Trade(O);\nvalue(T)\n\n# output\n\n11021.778063564074\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.Trade"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.Position","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"Position\n\nA netted position in a single instrument (identified by instrument_key). All fills on the same instrument aggregate here:\n\nnet_qty     — signed open quantity; the position is closed when this reaches 0.\navg_cost    — weighted-average per-unit entry price, in the price(derivative)                 convention (raw, excluding fees).\nrealized_pnl— realized trading P&L net of all commissions and slippage charged on                 this instrument.\nloan        — broker-financed dollar amount still owed against this position (0.0                 unless opened under a margin model with initial_margin_pct < 1.0).\n\nFees are not folded into avg_cost (so mark-to-market basis stays clean); they are subtracted from realized_pnl as they occur. Equity (cash + Σ value(P) - Σ loan) is the source of truth and already reflects fees via the cash ledger.\n\nA = asset()\nP = Position(Buy(A, 0))\napply_trade!(P, 10.0, value(A), 0.0)   # open 10 @ spot\nis_closed(P)\n# output\n\nfalse\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.Position"},{"category":"function","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.apply_trade!","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"apply_trade!(P::Position, qty::Real, fill_price::Real, fee::Real=0.0; borrowed::Real=0.0)\n\nFold a fill of signed qty units at per-unit fill_price (raw, fee-exclusive) into the netted position. fee is the total commission+slippage on the fill; it is subtracted from realized_pnl. borrowed is the broker-financed dollar amount of this fill (0.0 unless opening/adding under a margin model) — see loan on Position.\n\nAdding (same sign / opening): updates the weighted-average avg_cost and accumulates loan += borrowed.\nReducing/closing (opposite sign): realizes P&L on the closed quantity and repays loan proportionally to the fraction of the position closed. If the fill flips the position through zero, the remainder opens a fresh lot at fill_price (with loan == 0.0, since the proportional repay above already drove it there on a full close).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.apply_trade!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.request_to_close-Tuple{Position}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"request_to_close(P::Position)\n\nSet the position's close flag. To have the broker actually close it, request the close through the broker API (request_to_close_all!/request_to_close!), which also arms the broker's per-bar resolve; resolve_portfolio! skips its scan unless a broker-level close was requested.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.request_to_close"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.Portfolio","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"Portfolio\n\nNetted positions grouped by concrete derivative type. groups is a Vector of Group{D} objects (one per distinct derivative type — typically 1–2), held behind Any so the container is open to user-defined derivative types. A bare Vector, not a Dict: per-bar iteration is a direct 1–2 element walk (no hash-slot scan), and per-order type lookup is a short linear scan that beats hashing a DataType. n caches the total open-position count for O(1) length; _acc is a reused scratch accumulator so the per-group barrier returns nothing (no boxed return).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.Portfolio"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.get_or_create!-Union{Tuple{D}, Tuple{Portfolio, InstrumentKey, D}} where D<:Derivative","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"get_or_create!(pf, key, der::D) -> Position{D}\n\nReturn the live Position{D} for key, creating an empty one on first fill. Type-stable in D (caller passes a concrete derivative), so the returned position is concrete.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.get_or_create!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.has_position-Tuple{Portfolio, String}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"has_position(pf::Portfolio, ticker::String) -> Bool\n\nReturn true if the portfolio holds any open position (long or short) in ticker. Barrier per type-group; allocation-free.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.has_position"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.position_direction-Tuple{Portfolio, String}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"position_direction(pf::Portfolio, ticker::String) -> Symbol\n\nReturn :long, :short, or :flat for the first open position in ticker (walk order matches values(pf)). Barrier per type-group; allocation-free.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.position_direction"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.total_loan-Tuple{Portfolio}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"total_loan(pf::Portfolio) -> Float64\n\nSum of P.loan over all open positions — the aggregate broker-financed debt outstanding. Structurally identical to total_value (same union-split, allocation-free walk); always 0.0 unless positions were opened under a margin model with initial_margin_pct < 1.0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.total_loan"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.total_value-Tuple{Portfolio}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"total_value(pf::Portfolio) -> Float64\n\nSum of value(P) over all open positions. The per-group barrier writes into _acc and returns nothing (no boxed return); the inner loop is a contiguous, allocation-free scan.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.total_value"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.Broker","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"Broker(market::Market, cash::Real; cost_model::CostModel=NoCost(), margin_model::MarginModel=NoMargin())\n\nThe order-executing unit of the system. Holds cash, a Market, a pluggable transaction cost_model, a pluggable margin_model, a netted portfolio (keyed by instrument_key), the open orders queue (FIFO), the executed-trade history, a list of rejected orders, a list of margin_calls (bar indices where a maintenance breach forced a full liquidation), and the equity_history.\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nx=asset();\ny=asset();\nM=Market([x,y]);\nB = Broker(M,1000);\nisa(B,Broker)\n# output\n\ntrue\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.Broker"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.accrue_borrow_fee!-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"accrue_borrow_fee!(B::Broker)\n\nCharge one bar's worth of borrow_rate(B.margin_model) interest against every open position's financed exposure — abs(value(P)) for a short, P.loan for a margin-financed long. No-op under NoMargin (or any model with borrow_rate == 0.0).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.accrue_borrow_fee!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.cash_history-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"cash_history(B::Broker)\n\nReturn the cash history of the Broker\n\nExample\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nM=market([asset(),asset()]);\nT = Backtest(M,CrossOverStrategy,1000)\nrun_test(T)\ncash_history(T.broker)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.cash_history"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.check_margin!-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"check_margin!(B::Broker)\n\nIf account equity (cash + total_value(portfolio) - total_loan(portfolio)) falls below the aggregate maintenance requirement (Σ abs(value(P))*maintenance_margin_pct(B.margin_model)), records the bar in B.margin_calls and liquidates the whole book via request_to_close_all!/resolve_portfolio!. No-op under NoMargin (or any model with maintenance_margin_pct == 0.0).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.check_margin!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.execute!-Union{Tuple{K}, Tuple{D}, Tuple{Broker, Order{D, K}}, Tuple{Broker, Order{D, K}, Int64}} where {D<:Derivative, K<:OrderKind}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"execute!(B::Broker, O::Order, date::Int=length(B); strict::Bool=false)\n\nThe single fill path used by every order-processing function. Checks whether O triggers on date via check_trigger — market orders always do, limit/stop orders only when the bar's range reaches their trigger price. On trigger, resolves how much cash this fill actually needs:\n\nA same-direction long open/add (adding to or opening a position in the same direction as the fill) is margin-financeable: only notional*initial_margin_pct(B.margin_model) + fee is drawn from cash, the rest is broker-financed (Position.loan).\nA same-direction short open/add requires abs(notional)*short_margin_rate(B.margin_model) cash on hand as a pre-condition (no financing — proceeds still credit in full, as always).\nA reducing or flipping fill (opposite sign of the position's net_qty) is never margin-financed — full notional+fee required, exactly the pre-margin formula. Any outstanding loan on the position is repaid proportionally to the fraction closed.\n\nWith B.margin_model = NoMargin() (the default), initial_margin_pct == 1.0 and short_margin_rate == 0.0 reproduce today's exact formulas for both sides.\n\nInsufficient funds are recorded in B.rejected, unless strict=true, in which case they error — unless O.allow_partial is set, in which case the affordable fraction fills instead and the order stays open in the book for the remainder. A resting, untriggered limit/stop order is left untouched (not fulfilled, not rejected).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.execute!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.has_position-Tuple{Broker, String}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"has_position(B::Broker, ticker::String) -> Bool\n\nReturn true if the broker currently holds any open position (long or short) in ticker.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.has_position"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.place_order!-Tuple{Broker, Order}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"place_order!(B::Broker,O::Order)\n\nPlace an Order in the Broker's Orderbook\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nB = broker(3,1000);\nA = B.market.data[collect(keys(B.market.data))[2]]\nO = Order(Buy(A,10))\nplace_order!(B,O)\nB\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.place_order!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.position_direction-Tuple{Broker, String}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"position_direction(B::Broker, ticker::String) -> Symbol\n\nReturn :long, :short, or :flat for the current open position in ticker. Direction is taken from the sign of value(P) so it is correct for both Buy/Sell legs and options.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.position_direction"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.process_last_order!-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"process_last_order!(B::Broker)\n\nPop and fill the most recently placed order via execute! (strict=true).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.process_last_order!"},{"category":"function","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.process_order!","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"process_order!(B::Broker, O::Order, check_books::Bool=true)\n\nStrictly process a single order: remove it from the orderbook (when check_books) and fill it via execute! with strict=true, so insufficient funds raise instead of being recorded as a rejection.\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nB = broker(3,1000);\nA = B.market.data[collect(keys(B.market.data))[2]]\nO = Order(Buy(A,10))\nplace_order!(B,O)\nprocess_order!(B,O)\nlength(B.history)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.process_order!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.process_orders!-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"process_orders!(B::Broker)\n\nProcess the whole orderbook in FIFO order via execute!. Orders that fully fill (the whole book, for plain market orders) or are rejected for insufficient funds are removed; resting limit/stop orders that don't trigger on this bar, and partially-filled orders with quantity still outstanding, stay queued for a future bar.\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nB = broker(3,1000);\nA = B.market.data[collect(keys(B.market.data))[2]]\nO = Order(Buy(A,10))\nplace_order!(B,O)\nprocess_orders!(B)\nlength(B.history)\n\n# output\n\n1\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.process_orders!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.realized_pnl-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"realized_pnl(B::Broker) -> Float64\n\nTotal realized trading P&L, net of all commissions and slippage, across open positions. Note: fully closed positions are dropped from the portfolio, so this tracks realized P&L still attached to live instruments.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.realized_pnl"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.request_to_close!-Tuple{Broker, String}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"request_to_close!(B::Broker, ticker::String)\n\nMark all open positions for ticker to be closed on the next process_all! call.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.request_to_close!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.request_to_close_all!-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"request_to_close_all!(B::Broker)\n\nFlag every open position to be closed on the next resolve_portfolio!/process_all!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.request_to_close_all!"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.resolve_portfolio!-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"resolve_portfolio!(B::Broker)\n\nClose every position whose requestToClose flag is set, liquidating at the current market value. Each close realizes P&L, applies transaction costs, books the cash, records a closing Trade, and removes the position from the portfolio. Forced — always executes.\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nB = broker(3,1000);\nA = B.market.data[collect(keys(B.market.data))[2]]\nO = Order(Sell(A,10))\nplace_order!(B,O)\nprocess_order!(B,O)\nrequest_to_close_all!(B)\nresolve_portfolio!(B)\nlength(B.history)\n\n# output\n\n2\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.resolve_portfolio!"},{"category":"function","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.status","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"status(B::Broker,digits::Int=2)\n\nPrint the status of the Broker\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nx=asset();\ny=asset();\nM=market([x,y]);\nB = broker(M,1000);\nstatus(B)\n\n# output\n\n========================================\nDate: 3651\nCash: 1000.0\nNumber of orders: 0\nNumber of positions: 0\nNumber of trades: 0\n========================================\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.status"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.to_index-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"to_index(B::Broker)::Asset\n\nConvert a Broker to an Asset\n\nRandom.seed!(1234);\nx=asset();\ny=asset();\nM=market([x,y]);\nB = broker(M,1000);\nBT = Backtest(M,CrossOverStrategy,1000)\nrun_test(BT)\nA = to_index(BT.broker)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.to_index"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.unrealized_pnl-Tuple{Broker}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"unrealized_pnl(B::Broker) -> Float64\n\nTotal unrealized P&L (mark minus cost basis) across all currently open positions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.unrealized_pnl"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.CostModel","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"CostModel\n\nAbstract type for transaction-cost models. A cost model maps the gross notional of a fill to a (commission, slippage) pair, both expressed as positive cash amounts that always worsen the fill (commission is paid, slippage is an adverse price move).\n\nImplement a new model by adding a transaction_cost(::MyCostModel, notional) method.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.CostModel"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.FlatCost","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"FlatCost(; commission_pct=0.0, slippage_bps=0.0)\n\nFlat proportional cost model.\n\ncommission_pct — commission as a fraction of |notional| (e.g. 0.001 = 10 bps).\nslippage_bps   — adverse fill as basis points of |notional| (e.g. 5.0 = 5 bps).\n\nBoth are charged on every fill regardless of trade direction.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.FlatCost"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.NoCost","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"NoCost()\n\nFrictionless fills — zero commission, zero slippage. The default so existing backtests behave exactly as before.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.NoCost"},{"category":"method","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.transaction_cost-Tuple{NoCost, Real}","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"transaction_cost(model::CostModel, notional::Real) -> (commission, slippage)\n\nReturn the (commission, slippage) cash amounts for a fill of the given gross notional. Both values are non-negative.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.transaction_cost"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.MarginModel","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"MarginModel\n\nAbstract type for margin/leverage models. Governs how much of a same-direction long open/add is cash-secured vs. broker-financed (initial_margin_pct), the cash required to open/add a short as a fraction of its notional (short_margin_rate), the account-level equity threshold below which the whole book is liquidated (maintenance_margin_pct), and the per-bar rate charged on financed-long and short exposure (borrow_rate).\n\ninitial_margin_pct and short_margin_rate are kept separate (not one shared \"leverage\" number) because NoMargin's today-behavior is asymmetric: longs are fully cash-secured (initial_margin_pct == 1.0, unchanged from before margin models existed) while shorts are entirely unconstrained (short_margin_rate == 0.0, also unchanged) — a single shared fraction couldn't represent both defaults at once.\n\nImplement a new model by adding methods for all four functions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.MarginModel"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.NoMargin","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"NoMargin()\n\nNo leverage, no liquidation, no borrow fee — the default, so existing backtests behave exactly as before margin models existed. Longs are fully cash-secured (initial_margin_pct == 1.0); shorts are unconstrained (short_margin_rate == 0.0, today's exact behavior); the maintenance check and borrow-fee accrual are no-ops.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.NoMargin"},{"category":"type","location":"core_accounting/#Orcus.RegTMargin","page":"Orders & accounting","text":"RegTMargin(initial_pct, maintenance_pct, borrow_rate)\n\nA configurable leverage model — not a regulatory-accurate Reg-T implementation, just named after the familiar initial/maintenance-margin shape. initial_pct governs leverage symmetrically for both same-direction long opens/adds (initial_margin_pct) and short opens/adds (short_margin_rate) — one number, two roles.\n\ninitial_pct     — fraction of notional that must be cash-secured on a same-direction long                      open/add (e.g. 0.5 → 2x leverage); the rest is broker-financed. For a                      short, the fraction of its notional that must be on hand to open it.\nmaintenance_pct — fraction of gross open position value that account equity must stay                      above; falling below it liquidates the whole book.\nborrow_rate      — per-bar rate charged on the broker-financed portion of margin longs                      and on the full notional of open shorts.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Orcus.RegTMargin"}]
}
